THOUGHT: startBlock is explicitly annotated @Nullable in FinallyExtractInfo, so passing it directly to searchFromFirstBlock (which expects a non-null BlockNode) triggers the PASS_NULLABLE error. The safe and simple fix is to add a null-check in searchDuplicateInsns: if startBlock is null, we cannot search for duplicate instructions, so we should return false before calling searchFromFirstBlock. This avoids changing other logic and should not introduce new errors. After that, I need to run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count decreases by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '339,343s/^/		/' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/visitors/finaly/MarkFinallyVisitor.java && sed -i '335,343s/.*/		private static boolean searchDuplicateInsns(BlockNode checkBlock, FinallyExtractInfo extractInfo) {
			boolean isNew = extractInfo.getCheckedBlocks().add(checkBlock);
			if (!isNew) {
				return false;
			}
			BlockNode startBlock = extractInfo.getStartBlock();
			if (startBlock == null) {
				return false;
			}
			InsnsSlice dupSlice = searchFromFirstBlock(checkBlock, startBlock, extractInfo);
			if (dupSlice == null) {
				return false;
			}
			extractInfo.getDuplicateSlices().add(dupSlice);
			return true;
		}/' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/visitors/finaly/MarkFinallyVisitor.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E 'NullAway: .*errors' -n new_build_output.log || sed -n '330,350p' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/visitors/finaly/MarkFinallyVisitor.java```

